{"availability":"available","full":"eattrenclenhard/Sho-Time","name":"Sho-Time","description":"A simple self-hosted web app for authorising selected Google API Oauth2 scopes. Supports Google Drive, Google Photos and Youtube","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":6,"forks":2,"created":"2025-01-29T22:01:46Z","updated":"2025-04-14T15:12:06Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://shotime.streamlit.app","topics":["google-cloud-api","google-oauth2","google-photos-api","python3","streamlit"],"demo":"https://shotime.streamlit.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T16:33:37.063Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T16:33:37.063Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T16:33:37.063Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T16:33:37.063Z","stars":6,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A simple self-hosted web app for authorising selected Google API Oauth2 scopes via self-defined API credentials. Supports Google Drive, Google Photos and Youtube.","This app provides an intuitive and a straightforward way for user to perform OAuth flow authorisation process to grant certain level of access to specific parts Google services via self-defined API client credentials to third party app such as rclone and alist etc.","Rclone hardcodes redirect URI to for Google Drive. This means that you'd always need to complete Oauth2 flow on another machine that has GUI environment. With this app, you can throw this concern out the window, you can complete your Oauth2 flow authentication of a new rclone remote remotely here, no machine GUI required. Besides that, you can customize each scope and its respective permission, providing fine-grained control over access."],"features":["supports headless machine, GUI environment is not required for completing OAuth 2.0 flow","self-hosted, full control over your own data","privacy-oriented, manually clear session anytime you want to start over or exit","clears record every 12 hours","cookie support, remembers last used state"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eattrenclenhard/Sho-Time/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8c4173c114892ba1468cbec831d35762b92a0d629cb2daac13a8bc00d31e616e","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T16:33:37.501Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T16:33:37.501Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A simple self-hosted web app for authorising selected Google API Oauth2 scopes via self-defined API credentials. Supports Google Drive, Google Photos and Youtube.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eattrenclenhard/Sho-Time/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Thus, I decided to take it upon my shoulders to provide a GUI option for users who wish to grant third party access to specific Google services but opt for custom API client instead. > [!IMPORTANT] > Please refrain from using the demo app I've deployed to generate access token, please deploy your own copy instead.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eattrenclenhard/Sho-Time/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"self-hosted, full control over your own data","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eattrenclenhard/Sho-Time/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Sign in or register here.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eattrenclenhard/Sho-Time/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"8c4173c114892ba1468cbec831d35762b92a0d629cb2daac13a8bc00d31e616e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eattrenclenhard/Sho-Time/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T16:33:37.501Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-04-14T15:12:06Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eattrenclenhard/Sho-Time/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T16:33:37.502Z","hash":"8c4173c114892ba1468cbec831d35762b92a0d629cb2daac13a8bc00d31e616e","originalBytes":5468,"storedBytes":5468,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["app","google","streamlit","access","client","image","over"